# NeuroGate 🧠🔓

**Open compliance & rights toolkit for neural data — governance + benchmarks for democratized BCI.**

> Your neural data never leaves your hands. This repo hosts no patient data. Ever.

## Why
Neural-data laws just landed (Colorado HB24-1058, California CPRA provisions, Chile's constitutional
neurorights amendment) — and **nobody ships practical tooling**. Meanwhile neural decoding has no
shared benchmark despite strong open formats (NWB, DANDI, BIDS). NeuroGate closes both gaps.

## 30 seconds to first value
```bash
pipx install neurogate     # or: pip install neurogate
neurogate init ~/my-dataset --owner "Your Name" --jurisdiction US-CA
neurogate check ~/my-dataset
neurogate bench            # run the open benchmark suite
```

## What it does
- **NDRM** — a tiny YAML sidecar (`ndrm.yaml`) declaring ownership, law packs, allowed uses,
  and revocation contact for any neural dataset. Commit it next to your data.
- **Law packs** — practical control checklists encoded from CO HB24-1058, CA CPRA neural-data
  provisions, Chile's Art. 19 neurorights amendment, GDPR Art. 9 analog.
- **Open decoder benchmarks** — the shared benchmark the field lacks; DANDI by reference,
  synthetic baselines runnable out of the box.

## Governance
Stewardship council, free forever, Apache-2.0 — see [GOVERNANCE.md](GOVERNANCE.md).

## Status
v0.1 alpha. Benchmark protocol definitions are seed-quality; the protocol specs cite
BrainGate yield data (35.6% mean initial yield) and Willett-2023 speech-decoding throughput.
